 "discussion": {
  "office": "SLC",
  "issued": "2026-11-22T18:42:00+00:00",
  "key_messages": "- A weak weather system will bring a chance of snow showers across higher terrain on Monday, with little accumulation. - Low chances for fog development will return Tuesday morning across prone areas such as the Cache Valley, depending on if low clouds can fully clear out Monday night. - Another weak system is forecast to cross the region on Thanksgiving. This will bring a small chance for valley rain and mountain snow to northern Utah, while southern Utah remains largely dry.",
